            <ArticleTitle>Genetic polymorphisms in chitinase 3-like 1 (CHI3L1) are associated with circulating YKL-40 levels, but not with angiographic coronary artery disease in a Chinese population.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>51-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.cyto.2010.12.018</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">We sought to examine if polymorphisms in the promoter region of YKL-40 gene (CHI3L1) are associated with serum YKL-40 levels and coronary artery disease (CAD) in Chinese patients.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">Three single nucleotide polymorphisms (SNPs) (-329G&gt;A, rs10399931; -247C&gt;T, rs10399805; -131G&gt;C, rs4950928) in the CHI3L1 promoter were determined in 213 consecutive patients with angiographically documented CAD (luminal diameter stenosis ≥50%) and 248 normal controls. Coronary cumulative obstruction score and number of diseased vessels represent the severity of CAD. Serum YKL-40 levels were assessed using an ELISA kit.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">Patients with CAD had remarkably higher serum YKL-40 levels compared to controls (p&lt;0.001). There was no difference in the allele, genotype and haplotype distribution of these three SNPs between controls and CAD patients. The minor alleles of CHI3L1-329G&gt;A and -131G&gt;C were significantly associated with decreased serum YKL-40 levels in both controls (p = 0.001 and p&lt;0.001, respectively) and CAD patients (p = 0.007 and p&lt;0.001, respectively), whereas CHI3L1-247C&gt;T had no appreciable effect. None of these genetic variants and haplotypes was associated with severity of angiographic CAD.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">CHI3L1-329G&gt;A and -131G&gt;C polymorphisms are associated with serum YKL-40 levels, but not with the prevalence or severity of CAD.</AbstractText>
